cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite the published strain-vorticity paper it
  extends (see `preferred-citation`), and, if you refer to the audit itself, this
  repository. The DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22675817 identifies the published paper, not
  this repository; this repository has no DOI of its own.
title: Strain-Vorticity Comparator Dynamics
abstract: >-
  Symbolic verification, numerical validation and adversarial audit of a coordinate
  framework for the local strain-rotation balance of incompressible three-dimensional
  flow, extending the strain-vorticity research program of the paper deposited at
  10.5281/zenodo.22675817. Establishes that the binary-partition altitude family is
  an exact two-to-one function of the signed allocation coordinate zeta and therefore
  discards one bit of orientation per state; that the exact enstrophy production
  factorizes as scale x allocation x alignment,
  P = ||grad u||^3 * 2 h^{3/2} * exp(xi/2) * A, with the sharp pointwise bound
  4 sqrt(2)/9 attained at zeta = 1/3; that the material evolution of the rapidity
  comparator xi = artanh(zeta) separates the local dynamics from the nonlocal
  pressure Hessian exactly, leaving the single deviatoric scalar S:H_dev/E_S; and,
  as a negative result within the tested local two-sector functional class and under
  a stated nondegeneracy condition, that exact elimination of the deviatoric
  pressure-Hessian contribution forces the functional to reduce effectively to a
  vorticity/enstrophy-only class. Includes 179 symbolic checks, exact
  counterexamples, random-field ensembles, restricted-Euler trajectories and 96^3
  direct numerical simulation checks. No claim of Navier-Stokes global regularity is
  made, and no new estimate, inequality, monotonicity result or closure theorem is
  claimed.
